<title>CHINA: STYLAND YEARLY NET RETURNS TO PROFIT.</title>
<headline>STYLAND YEARLY NET RETURNS TO PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.09 gain    vs 3.63 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  13.16 gain   vs 1.76 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    10.03 profit vs 27.96 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     110.51	 vs 74.00 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Styland Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Styland holds garment and consumer electronics firms.</p>
<p>In the current year, the gross proceeds from securities trading are excluded from turnover and the comparative figure for turnover in 1996 was adjusted to conform with the current year presentation.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$15.62 million on disposals of investment properties and leasehold land and building and loss of HK$2.45 million from bad debts written off</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
